### Analysis
# Union type breaks autocomplete for OpenAI provider options

**What fails:** The `openai` property in `RegisterProviderOptions` uses union type `OpenAIResponsesProviderOptions | OpenAIChatProviderOptions | OpenAICompletionProviderOptions`, which severely limits TypeScript autocomplete and type checking

**How to reproduce:**
```typescript
// In packages/openai/src/openai-provider.ts lines 264-267
declare module '@ai-sdk/provider-utils' {
  interface RegisterProviderOptions {
    openai?: OpenAIResponsesProviderOptions | OpenAIChatProviderOptions | OpenAICompletionProviderOptions;
  }
}
```

**Result:** TypeScript can only suggest properties that exist on ALL union members. Analysis shows only `logprobs` and `user` are common to all three types, while provider-specific options like `parallelToolCalls`, `reasoningEffort` (chat/responses only) and `echo`, `suffix` (completion only) become inaccessible

**Expected:** Per [TypeScript documentation](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/unions-and-intersections.html), union types only allow access to properties common to all members, confirming this design prevents the intended autocomplete improvements
</details>

