### Analysis
## Async `needsApproval` functions always evaluated as truthy\, causing all tools to require approval

**What fails\:** The `isApprovalNeeded()` function in `packages/ai/src/generate-text/is-approval-needed.ts` returns a Promise object when `needsApproval` is an async function\, instead of awaiting the result\. Since Promise objects are truthy in JavaScript\, any tool with an async `needsApproval` function is always treated as requiring approval\, regardless of the Promise\'s resolved value\.

**How to reproduce\:**

```typescript
const tool = {
  needsApproval: async (input) => {
    // Async check (e.g., database query)
    return false; // Should NOT require approval
  }
};

// In generate-text.ts or run-tools-transformation.ts:
if (isApprovalNeeded({ tool, toolCall, messages, experimental_context })) {
  // This always executes because Promise<false> is truthy
}
```

**Result\:** Tools with async `needsApproval` functions that return `false` incorrectly trigger approval requests\. Users implementing async approval logic \(database checks\, API calls\) cannot bypass approval even when their logic returns `false`\.

**Expected\:** The function should `await` the Promise and use the resolved boolean value\. Per the type signature in `packages/provider-utils/src/types/tool.ts` line 126\, `needsApproval` can return `boolean | PromiseLike<boolean>`\, and [MDN Promise documentation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise) confirms Promises must be awaited to access their resolved value\.

**Fixed in\:**

*   `packages/ai/src/generate-text/is-approval-needed.ts` \(made async\, added await\)
*   `packages/ai/src/generate-text/generate-text.ts` line 572 \(added await to call site\)
*   `packages/ai/src/generate-text/run-tools-transformation.ts` line 256 \(added await to call site\)

