  prompt: TEST_PROMPT,
  providerOptions: {
    anthropic: {
      container: {
        id: 'test-container-id',
        // No skills array or empty skills array
      },
    },
  },
});

// Expected: container field NOT included in request body, no beta headers added
// Actual (before fix): container field IS included, but beta headers are NOT added
```

**Root cause\:** Line 249 condition `...(anthropicOptions?.container && {...})` only checks if container exists\, not if it has skills\. The beta header logic \(lines 325\-332\) correctly checks `container.skills.length > 0`\, but the request body inclusion logic didn\'t match this condition\.

**Impact\:** Sending a container without skills \(or with empty skills array\) to the API without the corresponding required beta headers may cause the API to reject the request or behave unexpectedly\, since the container feature is specifically designed for skills support and requires those beta headers to function\.

**Fix\:** Updated line 249 to match the beta header condition\: container is now only included when both the container exists AND it contains skills with length \> 0\.

Reference\: [Agent Skills in Claude API docs](https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/quickstart) states that skills require specific beta headers for proper functionality\.

