const model = new OpenAICompatibleResponsesLanguageModel('text-davinci-003', {
  provider: 'openrouter.auto',
  headers: () => ({}),
  url: () => 'https://api.openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses',
});

// Call doGenerate or doStream
// Result: providerMetadata has keys 'openai' or 'providerOptionsName' 
// Expected: providerMetadata has key 'openrouter' (extracted from provider name)
```

**Result\:** When using non\-OpenAI providers like OpenRouter or xAI\, the providerMetadata is stored under incorrect keys\:

*   doGenerate content items have keys \"openai\" instead of the actual provider name
*   doStream events have keys \"providerOptionsName\" \(literal string\) or \"openai\" instead of the actual provider name
*   Final metadata in doStream has key \"providerOptionsName\" \(literal string\) instead of the actual provider name

**Expected\:** Per [SharedV3ProviderMetadata documentation](https://vercel.com/packages/provider/src/shared/v3/shared-v3-provider-metadata.ts)\, metadata should be keyed by the actual provider name extracted from the config\. For \"openrouter\.auto\"\, it should use \"openrouter\" as the key \(extracted via the providerOptionsName getter that splits on \'\.\' and takes the first part\)\.

**Fix\:** Replaced all hard\-coded `"openai"` keys and literal `"providerOptionsName"` keys with dynamic `[this.providerOptionsName]` in doGenerate\(\) and `[providerOptionsName]` in doStream\(\) to match the actual provider being used\.

