## Function tools incorrectly included when mixed with provider\-defined tools in Bedrock prepareTools

**What fails\:** The `prepareTools()` function in `packages/amazon-bedrock/src/bedrock-prepare-tools.ts` includes both provider\-defined tools \(Nova\/Anthropic\) and standard function tools in the same API request\, despite warning users that \"Only \[provider\] tools will be used\.\"

**How to reproduce\:**

```typescript
const result = await prepareTools({
  tools: [
    {
      type: 'provider-defined',
      id: 'nova.nova_grounding',
      name: 'nova_grounding',
      args: {},
    },
    {
      type: 'function',
      name: 'testFunction',
      inputSchema: { type: 'object', properties: {} },
    },
  ],
  modelId: 'us.amazon.nova-premier-v1:0',
});
```

**Result\:** `result.toolConfig.tools` contains 2 items\: one `systemTool` \(Nova\) and one `toolSpec` \(function tool\)\, contradicting the warning message\.

**Expected behavior\:** When provider\-defined tools \(Nova or Anthropic\) are mixed with function tools\, the warning message states \"Only \[provider\] tools will be used\.\" The function tools should be excluded from the output\, returning only the provider\-defined tools since Bedrock API does not support mixing tool types in a single call\.

**Root cause\:** Lines 179\-190 in bedrock\-prepare\-tools\.ts unconditionally add all function tools to the result regardless of whether `usingAnthropicTools` or `usingNovaTools` is true\. The same issue occurs for both Anthropic \(lines 90\-122\) and Nova \(lines 150\-176\) provider\-defined tools\.

**Fix\:** Wrap the function tools handling block in a condition to exclude function tools when using provider\-defined tools\:

*   Updated bedrock\-prepare\-tools\.ts line 179 to add condition\: `if (!usingAnthropicTools && !usingNovaTools)`
*   Updated bedrock\-prepare\-tools\.test\.ts to verify function tools are excluded in mixed scenarios
*   Added test case for Anthropic mixing scenario to match Nova test coverage

