  providerOptions: { blackForestLabs: { seed: null } },
  // ... other required params
});

// Current behavior: Request body includes {"seed": null}
// Expected behavior: seed field should be omitted from request body
```

**Result\:** When seed is explicitly set to null in providerOptions\, it gets serialized as `{"seed": null}` in the JSON request body\. Meanwhile\, all other 11 optional provider parameters \(prompt\_upsampling\, safety\_tolerance\, webhook\_url\, etc\.\) use `!= null` checks at lines 92\-110 to consistently omit null\/undefined values from the request body\.

**Expected\:** The seed parameter handling should match the established pattern for all other optional fields \- using a `!= null` check to omit null and undefined values\, ensuring consistent request body construction\.

