The structured-outputs-2025-11-13 beta header is only required by the direct Anthropic API, not by Bedrock. Structured outputs are GA on Bedrock and work without any beta header.
                                                                                                                                                                                                
From the https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/structured-output.html:        

Structured outputs is generally available in all commercial AWS regions for the select Amazon Bedrock serverless models.

The official Bedrock example uses output_config.format with no anthropic_beta in the request body:
```json
  {
    "anthropic_version": "bedrock-2023-05-31",
    "messages": [...],
    "max_tokens": 3000,
    "output_config": {
      "format": {
        "type": "json_schema",
        "schema": { ... }
      }
    }
  }
```
The extra anthropic-beta HTTP header that gets sent is harmless because Bedrock ignores unrecognized headers. This matches the behavior confirmed in the https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12298,
where @anthropic-ai/bedrock-sdk works with output_config.format and no beta.

