Tiny caveat here, [Bun currently does not support `hasSubscribers`](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/27805) on the top-level tracing channel instance.

So we usually either invert the check:

```ts
// only if we know for a fact there are zero subscribers, then we skip
if (tracingChannel?.hasSubscribers === false) {
  return await execute();
}
```

Or some other libs in the ecosystem iterate over the bundled channels to check there instead:

```ts
function hasSubs(channel: TracingChannel) {
  if (channel.hasSubscribers === undefined) {
    return ['start', 'end', 'error', 'asyncStart', 'asyncEnd'].some(c => channel[c].hasSubscribers);
  }

  return channel.hasSubscribers;
}
```

The first pattern is more common, and if there aren't any subscribers then the overhead is not a big deal in I/O heavy libs like AI SDKs.

